Description: Export GTK4 header bar menus to the Unity global menu
 GTK4 applications keep their menu in a header bar button rather than in a menu
 bar, so Unity's panel and HUD have nothing to show for them. GTK4 also removed
 the module loading mechanism that appmenu-gtk-module uses to reach GTK3
 applications, so the same approach cannot be taken.
 .
 This is a small LD_PRELOADable library instead. It finds the header bar's menu
 model through public GTK API and sets it as the application's menu bar before
 the window is realized, after which GTK4 exports it over org.gtk.Menus by
 itself. It does nothing outside a Unity session.
 .
 This package includes an environment variable snippet to load the library for
 all user processes. To disable it, create an empty file
 /etc/environment.d/60-unity-gtk4-menu.conf for everyone, or
 ~/.config/environment.d/60-unity-gtk4-menu.conf for one user.
